      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe, and I'd like you to confirm it first.\n\n- **Daily total:** 2000 mg three times daily is 6,000 mg/day. The usual maximum for adults is 4 g/day, and many institutions cap it at 3 g/day.\n- **Single dose:** 2000 mg is double the usual maximum single dose of 1000 mg. Even for a 70 kg adult with normal liver function, this carries a real risk of hepatotoxicity.\n\nHere are some options:\n1. **Acetaminophen 1000 mg PO three times daily.** This is 3 g/day and a common standard regimen.\n2. **Acetaminophen 1000 mg PO four times daily.** This is 4 g/day, the maximum, and is usually given at least 6 hours apart.\n3. **Acetaminophen 650 mg PO four times daily.** This is 2.6 g/day.\n\nIf 2000 mg TID is what you intend, for example as part of a protocol I don't know about, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording your confirmation. Otherwise, tell me which of the options above you'd like."
      }
     ],
