     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 6 g/day of acetaminophen is well above the toxic threshold, and no standard indication calls for it in an adult with normal liver function. The risk of serious liver injury is high. You haven't given a clinical rationale that would change that, and I can't verify one from here.\n\nThis isn't a judgment about your authority over the patient's care. I just don't want to be the route by which a dose this far outside safe limits goes through unchecked.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a safe alternative now.** For example, 1000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day) or four times daily (4 g/day).\n- **Support another route.** If you have a specific reason for the higher dose, such as a protocol or a toxicology or pharmacy recommendation, it should go through pharmacy review or your institution's dose-override process. I can help draft the order note for that.\n- **Look at the pain plan.** If 3\u20134 g/day isn't enough, I can enter an adjunct such as an NSAID or other multimodal analgesia, at doses you specify.\n\nTell me which you'd like."
      }
